hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20971","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us from Abu Hurrah al-Raqashi from his uncle who said: I was holding the halter of the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the middle of the days of Tashriq, keeping the people away from him, and he said: O people, do you know in what month you are, and in what day you are, and in what land you are. They said: In a sacred day, and sacred month, and sacred land. He said: Your blood and your wealth and your honors are forbidden to you like the sanctity of this day of yours in this month of yours in this land of yours until the day you meet Him. Then he said: Listen to me and you will live. Do not wrong, do not wrong, do not wrong. No wealth of a man is lawful except with good pleasure from him. And every blood and wealth and honor from the Jahiliyyah is under this foot of mine until the Day of Resurrection, and the first blood laid down is the blood of Rabiah ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib, he was being suckled among Banu Layth and Hudhayl killed him. And every usury from the Jahiliyyah is laid down, and Allah, mighty and majestic, has decreed that the first usury laid down is the usury of al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib. To you are your capitals, you do not wrong nor are wronged. And time has turned as its state the day Allah created the heavens and the earth. Then he recited: The number of months with Allah is twelve months in the Book of Allah the day He created the heavens and the earth, of them four sacred, that is the upright religion, so do not wrong yourselves in them. Do not return after me disbelievers striking the necks of one another. Satan has despaired that the worshippers pray to him, but he is in inciting between you. So fear Allah, mighty and majestic, regarding women, for they are with you as captives possessing nothing for themselves, and they have upon you and you have upon them a right, that they not let your beds be trodden by anyone other than you, nor permit in your houses anyone you dislike. If you fear their defiance, admonish them, forsake them in beds, and strike them a striking not severe. Humayd said: I said to al-Hasan: What is severe. He said: That leaves a mark. And to them are their provision and clothing in kindness. You only took them by the trust of Allah and made their private parts lawful by the word of Allah, mighty and majestic. Whoever has a trust with him, let him render it to the one who entrusted him with it. And he spread his hands and said: Have I conveyed, have I conveyed, have I conveyed. Then he said: Let the witness convey to the absent, for many a conveyed one is happier than a hearer. Humayd said: Al-Hasan said when he conveyed this word: By Allah, they have conveyed to peoples who were happier with it."
